			"notes": "Mostly Echoes, and a big speed fix.\n\n**Echoes got a makeover**\n\n- Panels are frosted glass now, tinted with the album cover's colours\n- New lines shoot out from your crosshair, and the words pop in one by one as they're sung. The rest of the line shows faintly so you can read ahead\n- When the next line comes in, the old one dims and slowly floats up\n- The panels are linked by a glowing thread, and little sparks and notes drift off the current line\n- Chorus lines (anything that repeats in the song) get a gold edge and a small \"chorus\" tag\n- A quick shine goes across a line when it finishes\n- Friends' Echoes panels use the same glass, in their own colour\n\n**It runs a lot faster**\n\nEchoes, vibe mode and some overlays were eating way too many frames. They're drawn a smarter way now. On one test machine the time Lyricraft takes to draw each frame went down by about 87% on average across every style and overlay, and by about 96% for the heavy ones (Echoes, vibe mode, vinyl and cassette). Echoes alone went from about 94 fps to 850 there. Your numbers will depend on your PC, but it should be a lot smoother. Nothing should look different, apart from the glow behind glowing words being a bit softer.\n\nSame requirements as before: Minecraft 26.3, Fabric Loader and Fabric API, Mod Menu optional. Just replace the old jar.\n\nIf something looks off or your fps is still bad with a certain style, open an issue and say which style/overlay you were using."
		},
