			"notes": "First release. Lyricraft shows the lyrics of whatever you're playing on Spotify while you play Minecraft, synced line by line. No Spotify login, it just reads what's playing on your computer.\n\nNeeds Minecraft 26.3, Fabric Loader and Fabric API. Mod Menu is optional. Drop the jar in your mods folder, play a song, press N for settings.\n\nWhat's in it:\n\n- 7 styles. Classic is the default, Echoes is the one I'd try first (every new line stays where you were looking, so you leave a trail of lyrics as you walk around)\n- Now Playing card with the album cover, 5 looks and 7 themes, and you can drag it anywhere\n- Vibe mode that tints the screen in the album's colours, plus 9 overlays (vinyl, cassette, VHS, lo-fi rain...)\n- Better timing: it combines every synced version of a song on LRCLIB instead of trusting one. If a song is still off, [ and ] nudge it and it remembers\n- Players who also have the mod get a green ♫ next to their name, their current line floats above their head, and if they use Echoes you see their panels too. Works on any server. You can turn all of it off in the Online tab\n\nWindows, macOS and Linux (Linux needs `playerctl`).\n\nProbably has a few rough edges, since it's the first version. If something breaks or a song never syncs right, open an issue and tell me the song."
